  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The LOD graphic setting for pc users is causing culling issues in my vrchat world if it is set to low or to medium where entire rooms disappear while players are standing in them. It seems vrchat is enforcing their own values onto the LOD component which quickly culls objects even when I set the LOD component to still display objects at that distance. It makes the LOD component uncontrollable and unusable if I want the PC players to still see the room they are standing in. A solution would be to make it so the LOD graphic setting does not modify the LOD component in regards to object culling so objects still cull at the distance they were set up by the world creator to cull at. I think I am just going to make my own script which will do exactly what the LOD component does except VRChat won't mess it up if the LOD graphic setting is set to low or medium. Love the platform, godspeed fellow code human.",
